---
description: KYRiE project-wide development rules
alwaysApply: true
---

- Preserve passive receive capture and existing SQLite columns.
- Add regression coverage for behavior changes; run only affected methods/modules by default.
- Use `python -m tools.run_tests --list` and select relevant feature groups; see tests/README.md.
- Broaden checks only for concrete dependencies, failures, or unresolved concerns. Run full discovery for releases or justified cross-cutting changes, not every edit.
- Report the scope actually run; never imply a selected run verified the full suite.
- Keep tests grouped by responsibility; retain useful regression coverage and avoid duplicate implementation-only checks.
- Packet IDs and variable lengths are little endian; lengths include headers.
- Duplicate definitions use the last entry. Never guess boundaries after unknown IDs.
- Keep framing, TCP assembly, IPC decoding and GUI responsibilities separate.
- Bound external buffers and fail the affected stream closed on invalid input.
- Synchronize capture state shared with process discovery; call UI through Qt signals.
- Missing bytes must wait for retransmission; never synthesize packet contents.
- Keep PacketEvent independent of Scapy, Qt and native pointer sizes.
- Never log plaintext payloads in diagnostic messages.
- Document native wire formats, ownership, shutdown and overflow behavior.
- Validate with synthetic traffic before authorized Windows/game integration tests.
- Prioritize Auriga NPC code restoration (including timed events) and MOB analysis, following MARiA's functionality.
- Keep rAthena rendering separate and lower priority; keep all wording in external profiles.
- Separate semantic/state analysis from text rendering and emulator-specific code generation.
- Preserve evidence for inferred timing, branches and skill statistics; never invent unseen server logic.
- Compute MOB skill intervals per individual before aggregating by class.
- Recognized initial HTTP traffic is PASS, not a game framing error; never scan unknown game bytes for synchronization.
